The conditions for auctioning land use rights when the state leases land with payment of usage fees and rents under the draft new regulation are:

(1) The bidder must meet the following conditions:
- They should be entities eligible for land leasing or rental according to Article 55 and Article 56 of the Land Law. Entities cannot form joint ventures or alliances to participate in auctions.
- They must fulfill the requirements stipulated in Article 14, Paragraph 2 of this regulation.
- They must comply with legal regulations regarding land use by the State for projects other than those being implemented.
- They must pay an advance deposit equivalent to 20% of the total value of the plot, area, and type of land listed at the starting price for the auction.

- They must pay an advance deposit equivalent to 20% of the total value of the plot, area, and type of land listed at the starting price for the auction;
- They must provide guarantees from banks to cover the investment required before project completion;
- They must not fall into categories explicitly prohibited from participating in auctions as specified in Point 6 of Article 6 of this regulation.

(2) Personal bidders who participate in land leasing bidding must meet the following criteria:
- Individuals who propose to lease land must have fulfilled all the provisions outlined in Points a, d, and e of this point;
- For individuals bidding to carry out real estate development projects, they must adhere to the provisions mentioned in Point 1 of this point.

(3) Rights and responsibilities of participants in land leasing bidding include:
- Being given full access to information related to the leased land;

(3) Rights and responsibilities of participants in land leasing bidding include:
- Being provided with complete details concerning the leased land during the auction;
- Having the right to withdraw from the bidding process if the starting price, location, area, or type of land has changed, along with any additional interest earned;
- Committing to completing the development plan approved at the time of the land leasing bid within the stated timeframe; 
